      "text": "To solve the given series \\(\\sum_{k = 1}^\\infty \\frac{6^k}{(3^k - 2^k)(3^{k + 1} - 2^{k + 1})}\\), we will use a method involving partial fraction decompositions and telescoping series.\n\nFirst, let's simplify the general term of the series:\n\\[\n\\frac{6^k}{(3^k - 2^k)(3^{k+1} - 2^{k+1})}.\n\\]\nNotice that \\(6^k = (2 \\cdot 3)^k = 2^k \\cdot 3^k\\). Therefore, the term can be rewritten as:\n\\[\n\\frac{6^k}{(3^k - 2^k)(3^{k+1} - 2^{k+1})} = \\frac{2^k \\cdot 3^k}{(3^k - 2^k)(3^{k+1} - 2^{k+1})}.\n\\]\nWe can further decompose this into partial fractions. Notice that:\n\\[\n\\frac{2^k \\cdot 3^k}{(3^k - 2^k)(3^{k+1} - 2^{k+1})} = \\frac{A}{3^k - 2^k} + \\frac{B}{3^{k+1} - 2^{k+1}}.\n\\]\nTo find \\(A\\) and \\(B\\), we clear the denominators:\n\\[\n2^k \\cdot 3^k = A(3^{k+1} - 2^{k+1}) + B(3^k - 2^k).\n\\]\nWe now equate the coefficients of like terms. From this equation, we get:\n\\[\n2^k \\cdot 3^k = A \\cdot 3^{k+1} - A \\cdot 2^{k+1} + B \\cdot 3^k - B \\cdot 2^k.\n\\]\nWe can set up the following system of equations by comparing coefficients:\n\\[\nA \\cdot 3^{k+1} + B \\cdot 3^k = 3^k \\quad \\text{(coefficient of } 3^k \\text{)}\n\\]\n\\[\n-A \\cdot 2^{k+1} - B \\cdot 2^k = 2^k \\quad \\text{(coefficient of } 2^k \\text{)}.\n\\]\nSolving these, we get:\n\\[\n3A = 1 \\implies A = \\frac{1}{3},\n\\]\n\\[\nB = -1.\n\\]\nSo, the partial fraction decomposition is:\n\\[\n\\frac{6^k}{(3^k - 2^k)(3^{k+1} - 2^{k+1})} = \\frac{1/3}{3^k - 2^k} - \\frac{1}{3^{k+1} - 2^{k+1}}.\n\\]\nThis gives us:\n\\[\n\\frac{6^k}{(3^k - 2^k)(3^{k+1} - 2^{k+1})} = \\frac{1}{3}( \\frac{1}{3^k - 2^k} - \\frac{1}{3^{k+1} - 2^{k+1}}).\n\\]\nThus, the series becomes a telescoping series:\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty \\left( \\frac{1}{3}( \\frac{1}{3^k - 2^k} - \\frac{1}{3^{k+1} - 2^{k+1}}) \\right).\n\\]\nWhen we expand the series, we see that most terms cancel out:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{3} \\left( \\left( \\frac{1}{3-2} - \\frac{1}{9-2} \\right) + \\left( \\frac{1}{9-4} - \\frac{1}{27-8} \\right) + \\left( \\frac{1}{27-8} - \\frac{1}{81-16} \\right) + \\cdots \\right).\n\\]\nAll terms cancel except the first term:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{3} \\left( \\frac{1}{3} - \\lim_{k \\to \\infty} \\frac{1}{3^{k+1} - 2^{k+1}} \\right).\n\\]\nSince \\(\\lim_{k \\to \\infty} \\frac{1}{3^{k+1} - 2^{k+1}} = 0\\), the series converges to:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{1}{9}.\n\\]\nTherefore, the sum of the series is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{9}}.\n\\]",
